  "editorial_blocks": [
    {
      "section": "3.6 Second target",
      "words": 167,
      "text": "[Placeholder \u2014 pending the second-target run.] To test whether the pipeline carries to another model, we apply it unchanged to a second target (gpt-oss-20b [@openai2025gptoss]) under a fixed-versus-varied protocol. Held fixed across targets: the scenario template, operator rule, and protected value; the forbidden-action rule decided from the tool log; the eligible-step window; the labels and the within scenario \u00d7 round metric; the detector recipes; and the matched controls. Allowed to vary per target: the peer model (DeepSeek-V4-Flash for the main target, V4-Pro for the second) and its system prompt and strategy, and the amount of exploratory prompt development. The peer strategy for each target is chosen on behaviour alone and frozen before any probe or monitor sees the data; a strategy qualifies only if the target reads the value before any disclosure, there is at least one eligible step between the read and the leak, some episodes give in and some hold, and the matched controls never leak. [Results and the full fixed-versus-varied table: \u00a74 and appendix.]",
      "position": {
        "page": 6,
        "y": 446.618,
        "end_page": 6,
        "end_y": 473.218,
        "end_char": 13100
      }
    },
